{"entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "primaryAccession": "P49573", "secondaryAccessions": ["D6W4C2"], "uniProtkbId": "CTR1_YEAST", "entryAudit": {"firstPublicDate": "1996-02-01", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2026-09-02", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "1996-02-01", "entryVersion": 188, "sequenceVersion": 1}, "annotationScore": 5.0, "organism": {"scientificName": "Saccharomyces cerevisiae (strain ATCC 204508 / S288c)", "commonName": "Baker's yeast", "taxonId": 559292, "lineage": ["Eukaryota", "Fungi", "Dikarya", "Ascomycota", "Saccharomycotina", "Saccharomycetes", "Saccharomycetales", "Saccharomycetaceae", "Saccharomyces"]}, "proteinExistence": "1: Evidence at protein level", "proteinDescription": {"recommendedName": {"fullName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "source": "PubMed", "id": "8293472"}], "value": "Copper transport protein CTR1"}, "shortNames": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "source": "PubMed", "id": "8293472"}], "value": "Copper transporter 1"}]}}, "genes": [{"geneName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "source": "PubMed", "id": "8293472"}], "value": "CTR1"}, "orderedLocusNames": [{"value": "YPR124W"}], "orfNames": [{"value": "P9642.3"}]}], "comments": [{"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "12370430"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "12391279"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "14511662"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "15012137"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "7929270"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "8293472"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "8756349"}], "value": "High-affinity copper transporter of plasma membrane that mediates copper uptake under low copper conditions (PubMed:12391279, PubMed:7929270, PubMed:8293472, PubMed:8756349). Copper transport through the high affinity system requiring CTRl supplies the iron transport multicopper ferroxidase FET3 with copper, which in turn is required for ferrous iron uptake (PubMed:8293472). The energy for translocation is unlikely to be directly derived from ATP hydrolysis and the exact mechanism driving the transmembrane transport of copper has still to be determined (PubMed:7929270). Binds 4 copper ions via its C-terminal cystein-rich domain and is able to deliver Cu(I) directly to both the chaperone ATX1 and to an N-terminal domain of the CCC2 protein (PubMed:15012137). Also able to mediate the uptake of the anticancer drug cisplatin (PubMed:12370430, PubMed:12391279, PubMed:14511662)"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION"}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "Cu(2+)(in) = Cu(2+)(out)", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:28703"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:29036"}], "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "12391279"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "7929270"}]}, "physiologicalReactions": [{"directionType": "right-to-left", "reactionCrossReference": {"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:28705"}, "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "12391279"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "7929270"}]}]}, {"commentType": "BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES", "kineticParameters": {"maximumVelocities": [{"velocity": 169.5, "unit": "nmol/min/mg", "enzyme": "enzyme towards copper", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "12391279"}]}, {"velocity": 76.9, "unit": "nmol/min/mg", "enzyme": "enzyme towards cisplatin", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "12391279"}]}], "michaelisConstants": [{"constant": 128.8, "unit": "uM", "substrate": "copper influx", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "12391279"}]}, {"constant": 140.2, "unit": "uM", "substrate": "cisplatin influx", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "12391279"}]}]}}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "7929270"}], "value": "Homooligomer"}], "commentType": "SUBUNIT"}, {"commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION", "subcellularLocations": [{"location": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "8293472"}], "value": "Cell membrane", "id": "SL-0039"}, "topology": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255"}], "value": "Multi-pass membrane protein", "id": "SL-9909"}}]}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "10480908"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "10922376"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "12011036"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "7929270"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9188496"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9211922"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9599102"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9726991"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9867833"}], "value": "Expression is induced by copper deprivation, and repressed by copper sufficiency (PubMed:7929270). Expression is regulated by the copper ion-sensing transcription factor MAC1 through the cis-acting copper ion-responsive element 5'-TTTGCTCA-3', termed CuRE, present in its promoter (PubMed:10480908, PubMed:10922376, PubMed:12011036, PubMed:9188496, PubMed:9211922, PubMed:9599102, PubMed:9726991, PubMed:9867833)"}], "commentType": "INDUCTION"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "8293472"}], "value": "Within the N-terminal cytosolic region appear three 19 amino acid repeated elements containing the M-X-X-M copper-binding motifs"}], "commentType": "DOMAIN"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "12011036"}], "value": "The REP-III motif within the C-terminal cytosolic part resembles a shortened MAC1 copper ion-sensing motif (REP) and plays a role in the CTR1 degradation"}], "commentType": "DOMAIN"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "7929270"}], "value": "Extensively O-glycosylated"}], "commentType": "PTM"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11557497"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "12370430"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "7929270"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "8293472"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "8756349"}], "value": "Reduces copper uptake and leads to altered cellular responses to extracellular copper such as deficient and copper and zinc superoxide dismutase activity (PubMed:7929270, PubMed:8756349). Results in profound deficiency in ferrous iron uptake (PubMed:8293472). Results in increased cisplatin resistance and reduced intracellular accumulation of cisplatin (PubMed:12370430). Exhibits marked sensitization to oxytetracycline (OTC) and doxycycline (DOX) (PubMed:11557497)"}], "commentType": "DISRUPTION PHENOTYPE"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "12011036"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "8670854"}], "value": "CTR1 undergoes MAC1-dependent degradation at the membrane in cells exposed to high copper levels and in a fashion independent of endocytosis"}], "commentType": "MISCELLANEOUS"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "14562106"}], "value": "Present with 1180 molecules/cell in log phase SD medium"}], "commentType": "MISCELLANEOUS"}], "features": [{"type": "Chain", "location": {"start": {"value": 1, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 406, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "de